[[0,311417,0,2,6,-4,"2015-07-19T17:57:10","kingemocut","",[],"<h2><strong>this question is mainly for <a href=\"https://voat.co/user/atko\">@atko</a> and <a href=\"https://voat.co/user/PuttItOut\">@PuttItOut</a>, but can be answered by anyone.</strong></h2>\n<p>A lot of us came here because of the stupid crap happening on the other site. we also came here because we liked how transparent the admins are. and now, while the site is currently invite only, i ask you why? is it because of <a href=\"https://41.media.tumblr.com/a5a6591e902d556777d5376feb52a64c/tumblr_n83aisQQuv1rtcs0eo1_500.jpg\">one troll</a> or is it because of the EU's ruling that anything a user says makes the <a href=\"http://technologyandoutsourcingblog.fieldfisher.com/2015/european-court-of-human-rights-rules-that-news-site-delfi-is-liable-for-users-comments\">site liable</a>. Maybe it's because you want to make sure that the servers don't end up <a href=\"http://blog.clairepeetz.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/01/Server_room_fire.jpg\">Like this</a>, or maybe it's something different entirely. but whatever it is, <a href=\"https://voat.co/user/atko\">@atko</a> and <a href=\"https://voat.co/user/PuttItOut\">@PuttItOut</a>, i ask that you tell the community about it, else i can bet a fair few users would be more iffy around you, and for a site that is still a rather small fish in a large pond is not something you would want to risk.</p>","Why is Voat.co currently invite only?","","AskVoat"],[1,1167966,0,1,0,1,"2015-07-19T17:58:35","ec69f4c200b442f59e9f","",[],"<p>I think it is a temporary measure to ensure the site stays up. </p>"],[2,1168041,1167966,0,1,-1,"2015-07-19T18:01:10","kingemocut","",[],"<p>that's likely, hence why i did say that in the submition body, but it'd be nice to have the admins tell us why. i would have expected them to have had an announcement about it at least</p>"]]
